1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,060
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,140
=Episode 6=

3
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:17,700
Mom?

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,260
Aren't you on the morning shift today?

5
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,260
I took the day off.

6
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:22,940
Since you're up,

7
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:23,860
come have breakfast.

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,420
(Luo Xiyu - 2014 Central Dance Academy
Entrance Exam Admission Ticket)

9
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,820
You're not going anywhere today.

10
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:45,820
Mom,

11
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,060
dancing is my dream.

12
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,860
Why do you have to stop me?

13
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:50,740
Your dream?

14
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,460
Dreams are impractical.

15
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,140
Your grades are so good.

16
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,380
You should aim for the best university.

17
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,300
You'll have a real future there.

18
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:58,740
Get a good job.

19
00:00:58,980 --> 00:00:59,700
Live a stable life.

20
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,220
If I do what you want
and aim for Tsinghua or Peking,

21
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:02,820
I'll just end up choosing

22
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,740
some major that matches my score
and drifting through it.

23
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:06,260
Mom,

24
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,660
I love dancing.

25
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,980
Can't you just let me do what I love?

26
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,420
There are so many dancers.

27
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:13,420
How many ever become truly great?

28
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:14,940
Ms. Lin was good enough, wasn't she?

29
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:16,900
Did she ever make it big onstage?

30
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,420
Now she teaches classes.

31
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:19,900
You spend half your life
chasing a dream,

32
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:20,780
and one wrong move

33
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:21,940
can leave you injured for life.

34
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:23,580
I'm willing to take that risk!

35
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:25,740
Mom,

36
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:28,260
I've listened to you my whole life.

37
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:30,460
But I only get one chance
to choose my college path!

38
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,060
I want to decide for myself!

39
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:32,980
Mom,

40
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,700
I know I can become
a principal dancer...

41
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,660
I'm your mother.

42
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:38,060
I can't just watch you
make the wrong choice.

43
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:39,380
That's enough.

44
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:40,380
Eat.

45
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,020
I'm not hungry anymore.

46
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:55,500
(07:30)

47
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:04,700
(Xiaoba)
(Emergency! I need your help!)

48
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,340
Hello?

49
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:13,580
Dr. Zhang.

50
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,620
(Dr. Luo,)

51
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,460
(your patient just came into the ER.)

52
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,740
(She said she couldn't find you.)

53
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,300
What happened?

54
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:20,260
(Looks like)

55
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:22,140
(she is vomiting blood after surgery
for a perforated stomach.)

56
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:23,100
(You need to come in right away.)

57
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,340
Okay.

58
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,180
I'm coming now.

59
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:38,860
Sir,

60
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,820
my cousin is locked inside her room.

61
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:41,740
We can't get in,

62
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:42,380
and she can't get out.

63
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:43,060
Don't worry.

64
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,940
If you don't mind me breaking the lock,
it'll be quick.

65
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,820
That's fine. Go ahead.

66
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:52,780
Got your ID,

67
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:53,780
leotard, and shoes?

68
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:54,660
Everything's ready.

69
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:55,340
It's already eight.

70
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,260
Can you make it by bike?

71
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:57,380
My mom took the bike.

72
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:58,180
I'll have to get a cab.

73
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:58,820
Can you even get one?

74
00:02:58,820 --> 00:02:59,740
Traffic was awful on the way here.

75
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:00,300
It's the only way.

76
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:00,980
I'm leaving now.

77
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:18,940
Get on.

78
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,260
You can ride a motorcycle?

79
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,780
I'm eighteen. I have a license.

80
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,260
Hurry!

81
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:32,020
(Yucai High School)

82
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:39,300
Since your exam went well today,

83
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,380
I'll treat you to a feast.

84
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,700
Why aren't you eating?

85
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,380
I ate a lot this morning.

86
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,220
I'm still full.

87
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,820
(Lime-Flavored Chips)

88
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,100
Are you ready?

89
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,380
When you get home,

90
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,860
it's going to be one hell of a storm.

91
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,500
As far as your mom knows,

92
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,140
you had Zhang Jinghang's mom

93
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:58,780
fake being sick

94
00:03:58,900 --> 00:03:59,700
to help cover for you.

95
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,140
And you had the lock broken.

96
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,820
That storm

97
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,380
was coming sooner or later anyway.

98
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:06,700
No matter what,

99
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:07,860
it's my life,

100
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,820
and I get to decide how to live it.

101
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:14,500
Okay.

102
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,980
Then before the storm hits,

103
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:19,780
is there anywhere you want to go?

104
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:21,540
Let me think.

105
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:25,220
The sunset is beautiful.

106
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:28,500
I hope that every day we're together,

107
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:31,220
I can watch the sunset with you.

108
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:43,020
Are you cold?

109
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,100
Yeah.

110
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:45,500
Wait here.

111
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:46,740
I'll get you a jacket.

112
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:47,620
Okay.

113
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,180
(I can't let things keep
going like this.)

114
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:01,900
(Otherwise, in the end,)

115
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:02,700
(I'll die again.)

116
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:05,620
You decided that fast?

117
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:07,580
I'm not going anywhere.

118
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:09,300
I'm going home.

119
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:10,980
I'm leaving!

120
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:11,860
You can head back on your own!

121
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,020
Lend me two yuan.

122
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:19,660
For what?

123
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:20,660
The bus.

124
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:21,940
Huh?

125
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,460
(A new week begins.)

126
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,220
(Temperatures have been
fluctuating lately,)

127
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,220
(with big swings between day and night.)

128
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,700
Her voice is already getting
on my nerves.

129
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:38,300
Why do I feel like

130
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:41,220
things have been kind of weird
between you and He Lan lately?

131
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,540
It's been all morning,

132
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,580
and you haven't said a word to him.

133
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:45,340
I...

134
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:47,260
I just feel like lately

135
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,460
I've gotten a little too close to him.

136
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:49,980
I don't want him to get the wrong idea.

137
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:51,740
Xiyu,

138
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:52,740
you know

139
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,860
I'm always on your side, no matter what.

140
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:55,620
But...

141
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,540
after everything He Lan's done for you,

142
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:59,300
this is kind of heartless,
don't you think?

143
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:10,380
Song Shuqi,

144
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:12,420
give me back my fountain pen, please.

145
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,180
Who says this pen is yours?

146
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,020
Your name isn't on it.

147
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,580
My mom had it custom-made for me

148
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,340
when she was abroad on business.

149
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,180
My initials are engraved inside.

150
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,660
(HXY)

151
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,180
Wow, impressive.

152
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,860
Your mom had it custom-made abroad?

153
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:36,260
Stop showing off.

154
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:38,340
You really think your mom
cares about you?

155
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,100
If she actually cared,

156
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,580
she wouldn't have dumped you on your dad

157
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,300
and gone abroad by herself.

158
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,100
You don't get to talk about my mom.

159
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:48,180
Just give me my pen back.

160
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,780
And what if I don't?

161
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,300
What are you gonna do about it?

162
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:56,740
Getting brave now, huh?

163
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,020
I'm already in a bad mood today.

164
00:06:59,060 --> 00:06:59,980
And you...

165
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:00,900
are really asking for it.

166
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:02,740
Want your pen?

167
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:04,620
Then...

168
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:06,300
come get it yourself.

169
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:11,420
You actually came to get it?

170
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:12,260
Fine.

171
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:13,140
Here you go.

172
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,060
Song Shuqi!

173
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,140
What are you doing?

174
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:21,620
He Xiaoyun

175
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:22,980
was getting in the way

176
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,220
while I was working.

177
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:26,140
The whole school just heard
everything you did.

178
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,620
The dean wants you
in the discipline office.

179
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:28,780
Impossible.

180
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,660
I turned the mic off!

181
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:36,940
Song Shuqi got busted live on air.

182
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:37,740
That was so satisfying!

183
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:38,900
Was that you?

184
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:46,660
Didn't you help He Xiaoyun before?

185
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:49,060
Song Shuqi got red ink on her pants,

186
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:50,540
and you lent her your sweatpants.

187
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:52,740
I think so.

188
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:55,140
But what happened today...

189
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:57,500
I honestly don't know who did it.

190
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:58,740
True.

191
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,420
He Xiaoyun's way too timid.

192
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:02,220
She'd never dare.

193
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:04,940
Looks like our school

194
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,980
has its own Zorro fighting for justice.

195
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,220
Who could it be?

196
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:17,340
Thank you for helping me.

197
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,060
I baked some cookies.

198
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:20,140
They're for you.

199
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:23,740
You don't have to thank me.

200
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:25,980
You should thank yourself
for standing up for yourself.

201
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:27,940
(Do you want your fountain pen back?)

202
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,660
(You don't want Song Shuqi
bullying you forever, do you?)

203
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,100
But...

204
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:00,660
if it weren't for you,

205
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,460
I wouldn't have had the courage.

206
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,220
I...

207
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,900
I need to make one thing clear.

208
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:09,020
I didn't punish Song Shuqi for you.

209
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:13,340
Also,

210
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:15,860
don't ever trust a bad person,

211
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:18,620
and don't go looking for someone
even worse to help you.

212
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:20,500
You happened to meet me.

213
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:22,380
You just got lucky.

214
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,340
(Luo Xiyu,)

215
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:33,300
(He Lan,)

216
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,300
(I'll make you both pay.)

217
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:37,580
Luo Xiyu.

218
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,420
How long are you going
to keep avoiding me?

219
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:51,220
I'm not avoiding you.

220
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:54,060
We were only ever

221
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,380
classmates anyway.

222
00:09:57,820 --> 00:10:00,020
Do you have to keep saying
we're "just classmates"?

223
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:03,940
You were behind what happened
to Song Shuqi, weren't you?

224
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:07,420
You really don't need to do things
like that for me.

225
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,740
We're from two different worlds.

226
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,540
I know...

227
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,540
you've done a lot for me,

228
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:15,620
and I'm really grateful.

229
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,500
But from now on,

230
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,620
I think we should keep our distance.

231
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:23,340
Call me heartless if you want.

232
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:24,940
You're overthinking it.

233
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:27,940
I just felt bad for He Xiaoyun.

234
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:28,660
And

235
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:31,100
don't act like I'm pestering you.

236
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,180
I'm not

237
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:34,780
that desperate.

238
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:09,330
♪I thought♪

239
00:11:09,330 --> 00:11:12,260
♪If we stayed apart a little longer♪

240
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,580
♪We'd each find our way♪

241
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:16,610
♪Into a brand-new world♪

242
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:19,010
♪But somehow, every time♪

243
00:11:19,010 --> 00:11:20,910
♪I meet you again♪

244
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:22,490
♪And every reunion becomes♪

245
00:11:22,490 --> 00:11:24,470
♪Another way of letting go♪

246
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,490
♪The promises♪

247
00:11:26,490 --> 00:11:29,440
♪We couldn't keep in this life♪

248
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,450
♪Why should♪

249
00:11:30,450 --> 00:11:33,750
♪We leave them for another life
to fulfill♪

250
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:36,140
♪But every time I leave you♪

251
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:37,950
♪There's always something left unsaid♪

252
00:11:37,950 --> 00:11:41,180
♪Farther, farther, farther away♪

253
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:45,870
♪Only to end up by your side again♪

254
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:48,140
♪I still can't let you go♪

255
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,320
♪I still can't let you go♪

256
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:54,520
♪Yet you won't let us love this way♪

257
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,610
♪If we can never be together♪

258
00:11:56,610 --> 00:11:58,870
♪If you don't want me to get hurt♪

259
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:00,250
♪Then why did you walk♪

260
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:03,140
♪Into this endless future of mine♪

261
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:05,290
♪I still can't let you go♪

262
00:12:05,290 --> 00:12:07,460
♪I still can't let you go♪

263
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:11,700
♪Yet you won't let us love this way♪

264
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,770
♪If we can never be together♪

265
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:16,070
♪If you don't want me to get hurt♪

266
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:19,780
♪Then why push away the moonlight♪

267
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:23,450
♪And pull me into your arms♪

268
00:12:42,250 --> 00:12:43,640
♪The promises♪

269
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,500
♪We couldn't keep in this life♪

270
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,630
♪Why should♪

271
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:49,790
♪We leave them for another life
to fulfill♪
